&lt;p&gt;Explanation of Revision: Based on Change Request (CR) 10901, the LCD was revised to remove all billing and coding and all language not related to reasonable and necessary provisions (&amp;ldquo;Bill Type Codes&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Revenue Codes&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;CPT&sol;HCPCS Codes&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;ICD-10 Codes that Support Medical Necessity&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Documentation Requirements&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Utilization Guidelines&amp;rdquo; sections of the LCD) and place them into a newly created billing and coding article. During the process of moving the ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes to the billing and coding article, the ICD-10-CM diagnosis code ranges were broken out and listed individually Also, the CMS IOM language has been removed from the LCD and instead, the IOM citation related to this language is referenced in the &amp;ldquo;CMS National Coverage Policy&amp;rdquo; section of the LCD. In addition, the Social Security Act, Code of Federal Regulations, and IOM reference sections were updated. The effective date of this revision is for claims processed on or after January 8, 2019 dates of service on or after October 3, 2018.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At this time 21st Century Cures Act will apply to new and revised LCDs that restrict coverage which requires comment and notice. This revision is not a restriction to the coverage determination and therefore not all the fields included on the LCD are applicable as noted in this LCD.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

